3.1 On $Z$, the functional $F(v)=-\int_{\Omega^-}
abla u_0^-\cdot
abla v^-$ is bounded by $\|
abla u_0^-\|_2a_Z(v,v)^{1/2}$. Apply [A2] to obtain a unique $z\in Z$ such that $a_Z(z,v)=F(v)$ for every $v\in Z$. Then $u=u_0+z\in\mathcal A_\phi$ satisfies $\int_{\Omega^-}
abla u^-\cdot
abla v^-+\int_{\Omega^+}
abla u^+\cdot
abla v^+=0$ for every $v\in Z$. For any $v\in Z$, expansion gives $\mathcal E(u+v)=\mathcal E(u)+\mathcal E(v)$, so $u$ is the unique minimizer and $\mathcal E(u)\le\mathcal E(u_0)$. Taking compactly supported tests inside either side proves weak harmonicity. [A2, step 1.1, step 2.1, given, construct]
